  "reasoning": "I treated the opening and the lecturer's explanation of why visual perception matters as the first closed sub-goal, because the opening must stay in the first segment and the lecturer explicitly moves to basic light behavior after sentence 38. I then cut at the clear topic bridges: light models to light-material interaction, color perception to eye physiology, eye physiology to visible light, visible light to central/peripheral vision, and vision types to the blind spot. Each segment names the concepts it relies on, so no merges were necessary. I kept sentence 187 with the blind-spot segment as a concluding remark and started the final segment at the explicit summary.",
